# Catalog Yield Forensics: Why Multi-SKU Packaging Outperforms Digital Velocity in Heritage Jazz

## Executive Summary

In the modern streaming landscape, legacy catalog valuation is too often judged by a single metric: velocity (weekly streaming counts and digital chart placement). However, a forensic analysis of Amazon jazz best-sellers reveals a structural market anomaly: Catalog Yield—driven by multi-format packaging, vinyl bundling, and physical collector editions—frequently out-earns high-velocity digital pure-plays in total top-line dollar generation.

For heritage labels like Blue Note, Verve, or Concord, the path to maximizing catalog ROI is not chasing low-margin digital streams, but engineering premium monetization architecture for high-intent collectors.

---

## Analytical Methodology & Data Architecture

To measure commercial extraction power beyond raw rank placement, we ingested digital and physical sales movement into DuckDB and defined a custom valuation metric: Catalog Yield Score.

Catalog Yield Score = Price (USD) * Formats Available
